\f0\fs24 \cf0 FIMPACT 10-year dataset \'96 README / Metadata\
\
File name:\
FIMPACT 10 year outcome all timepoints.xlsx\
\
Description:\
This file contains anonymised individual-level outcome data from the FIMPACT trial, covering all follow-up timepoints (up to 10 years). The dataset includes variables used in the primary and secondary analyses reported in the 10-year follow-up publication submitted to The BMJ.\
\
Contents:\
- One row per timepoint per participant (7 rows per participant: baseline, 3m, 6m, 12m, 24m, 60m, 120m)\
- Columns include:\
    - Treatment allocation (placebo, ASD or ET)\
    - Outcome variables (e.g. pain scores, functional scores, satisfaction)\
    - Age group (in 5-year intervals)\
    - Sex\
    - Follow-up timepoint\
    - Other derived variables used in analysis\
\
Anonymisation:\
All data are fully anonymised in accordance with GDPR and Finnish data protection regulations. The pseudonymisation key has been destroyed, and variables have been processed to ensure k-anonymity (minimum 6 individuals per stratum). Age is presented in groups, and no location or free-text data are included.\
\
Use:\
This dataset enables reproduction of the primary and secondary outcome analyses reported in the FIMPACT 10-year follow-up study. It is suitable for meta-analysis, secondary synthesis, or methodological research.\
\
Contact:\
Teppo J\'e4rvinen, MD, PhD\
teppo.jarvinen@helsinki.fi\
\
Variable descriptions:\
\
agr_group:\
  Age group at baseline (5-year intervals, e.g., 35\'9639, 40\'9644). Used for k-anonymisation; no exact ages included.\
\
Sex:\
  Biological sex of the participant (Male or Female).\
\
Patient#:\
  Randomly assigned anonymised participant ID. No identifying link exists.\
\
time:\
  Follow-up timepoint. One of: 0 (baseline), 3 (months), 6 (months), 12 (months), 24 (months), 60 (months), 120 (months).\
\
Study Group:\
  Randomisation group: ASD = Arthroscopic Subacromial Decompression; Placebo = Diagnostic arthroscopy; ET = Exercise therapy.\
\
As-treated group:\
  Treatment actually received, regardless of randomisation group (as-treated).\
\
Per-protocol indicator:\
  Binary variable indicating protocol adherence (1 = per-protocol, 0 = deviation).\
\
Pain VAS at rest:\
  Visual Analog Scale (0\'96100 mm) for shoulder pain at rest.\
\
Pain VAS on activity:\
  Visual Analog Scale (0\'96100 mm) for shoulder pain during activity.\
\
Constant Score:\
  Composite shoulder function score (0\'96100); higher scores indicate better function.\
\
SST_Score:\
  Simple Shoulder Test score (0\'9612); higher scores indicate better function.\
\
15D Score:\
  15D health-related quality-of-life score (0\'961 scale, 1 = full health).\
\
sf36_Physical_functioning:\
  SF-36 physical functioning subscale (0\'96100).\
\
sf36_mental_health:\
  SF-36 mental health subscale (0\'96100).\
\
sf36_General_health:\
  SF-36 general health subscale (0\'96100).\
\
Return to hobbies:\
  Binary indicator for return to previous hobbies (1 = returned, 0 = not returned).\
\
Responder:\
  Binary indicator for clinical responder status based on predefined thresholds.\
\
VAS_SatisfactionCare:\
  VAS score (0\'96100 mm) for participant\'92s satisfaction with received care.\
}